        "v": 5,
        "title": "Clarify knowledge.md auto-creation behavior in FAQ",
        "summary": "Updated FAQ copy in `web/src/lib/faq.tsx` to state that Codebuff \"typically\" will not create `knowledge.md` files, replacing absolute negation. This aligns documentation with observed agent behavior where file creation is heuristic rather than guaranteed. Scope limited to web frontend copy.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:58:20.555Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The help text on the website now says the assistant 'typically' won't create its own instruction files for you, rather than saying it will 'never' do so. This affects anyone reading the documentation to understand how the assistant handles these files, making the description more accurate to real-world behavior. If you looked at the FAQ today, you'd read slightly softer language that better reflects what actually happens.",
